00:45:33.673 --> 00:45:35.506
and it kind of turned out okay.

729
00:45:35.508 --> 00:45:38.177
- That's great.
- Yeah. and my memory's getting better.

730
00:45:39.804 --> 00:45:42.638
Good. well. the doctor didn't
say you were stuck. right?

731
00:45:42.640 --> 00:45:46.684
He said that your recovery
would be unpredictable.

732
00:45:46.686 --> 00:45:48.561
but there's always hope.

733
00:45:48.563 --> 00:45:49.979
- Yeah. I know.
- Yeah.

734
00:45:49.981 --> 00:45:53.649
Um. so. last night.
with that video game.

735
00:45:53.651 --> 00:45:57.113
it actually started making me remember
this other one. <i>Desert Duty.</i>

736
00:45:57.780 --> 00:46:02.366
So. I was thinking. um. just
maybe if I play that one again.

737
00:46:02.368 --> 00:46:04.203
it would actually help me remember more.

738
00:46:05.078 --> 00:46:08.039
- That's a shooter game. <i>Desert Duty</i>?
- Yeah. I know. Dad.

739
00:46:08.042 --> 00:46:10.251
But it's not like that. I just...

740
00:46:11.836 --> 00:46:13.880
There's something that I gotta remember.

741
00:46:17.091 --> 00:46:20.052
Yeah. buddy. I don't know.

742
00:46:22.471 --> 00:46:23.514
Yeah. no. I know.

743
00:46:25.099 --> 00:46:29.020
I get it. It was probably stupid anyway.

744
00:46:31.814 --> 00:46:34.150
- I should probably get some sleep.
- All right.

745
00:46:35.067 --> 00:46:36.736
- Night.
- Night.

746
00:46:41.282 --> 00:46:44.318
[OLIVIA] <i>But. kids. they don't always</i>

747
00:46:44.321 --> 00:46:46.496
<i>tell you everything they're feeling.</i>

748
00:46:56.672 --> 00:46:58.931
"I'm saying that the house is on fire.

749
00:46:58.932 --> 00:47:01.175
and all I know how to do is write poems.

750
00:47:01.177 --> 00:47:05.638
All I know how to do is arrange
flowers on the table of a burning home.

751
00:47:05.640 --> 00:47:09.060
I am pressing against the frame.
I am chanting the right words.

752
00:47:10.478 --> 00:47:12.855
I am gripping my fists
and letting them go."

753
00:47:13.981 --> 00:47:14.982
Wow.

754
00:47:16.651 --> 00:47:18.150
Hannah wrote that?

755
00:47:18.152 --> 00:47:19.693
I must have read it a million times.

756
00:47:19.695 --> 00:47:22.655
The whole time. I thought
it was about that school.

757
00:47:22.657 --> 00:47:26.200
The suffocating. oh. my God.
it's right there in front of me.

758
00:47:26.202 --> 00:47:29.121
The burning home. the flowers...

759
00:47:31.165 --> 00:47:32.750
It was about her dad's affair.

760
00:47:33.954 --> 00:47:35.668
There she was. trying to comfort me.

761
00:47:35.670 --> 00:47:37.294
when I should've been
trying to comfort her.

762
00:47:37.296 --> 00:47:38.879
I mean. why didn't I see it?

763
00:47:38.881 --> 00:47:41.548
Olivia. you can't blame
yourself. This is Andy's fault.

764
00:47:41.550 --> 00:47:44.178
Jackie. please don't tell
me how to feel right now.

765
00:47:49.266 --> 00:47:51.183
- I'm sorry.
- You're right.

766
00:47:51.185 --> 00:47:55.145
No. I'm sorry. It just... It's
more complicated than that.

767
00:47:55.147 --> 00:47:56.524
I didn't mean to overstep.

768
00:47:59.068 --> 00:48:01.944
You know. I think maybe
I should head to bed.

769
00:48:01.946 --> 00:48:04.363
- No. no. no.
- No. it's been a long day.

770
00:48:04.365 --> 00:48:06.409
Really. I need to get some rest.

771
00:48:07.535 --> 00:48:09.120
It was nice meeting you. Jessica.

772
00:48:22.179 --> 00:48:23.217
Well...

773
00:48:26.367 --> 00:48:27.596
[SIGHS DEEPLY]

774
00:48:29.598 --> 00:48:31.265
You must think I'm an idiot.

775
00:48:31.267 --> 00:48:33.561
wanting to protect a man
who doesn't deserve it.

776
00:48:35.060 --> 00:48:36.263
I get it.

777
00:48:37.648 --> 00:48:40.276
I mean. I really get it.

778
00:48:41.819 --> 00:48:43.193
You love him. right?

779
00:48:43.195 --> 00:48:47.491
Despite everything. and
it's crazy. but you love him.

780
00:48:49.772 --> 00:48:50.952
I do.

781
00:48:53.581 --> 00:48:55.583
Even though he hurt you so bad.

782
00:49:05.843 --> 00:49:07.386
You know. Jessica. if there's...

783
00:49:09.305 --> 00:49:11.682
If there's anything you
ever wanna talk about...

784
00:49:14.602 --> 00:49:17.146
Sometimes I think if Hannah
would have come to me.

785
00:49:19.982 --> 00:49:21.901
maybe things would have been different.

786
00:49:24.862 --> 00:49:27.615
Maybe it was too painful
for her to talk about it.

787
00:49:31.452 --> 00:49:33.996
Maybe she kept it all
in to protect herself.

788
00:49:37.458 --> 00:49:39.085
I'm not good at that.

789
00:49:40.377 --> 00:49:44.963
The more I think about
it. she was really brave.

790
00:49:44.965 --> 00:49:48.594
Oh. but. honey. we both
know that didn't work.

791
00:49:49.428 --> 00:49:50.554
Keeping it in.

792
00:49:52.014 --> 00:49:53.680
that's not brave.

793
00:49:53.682 --> 00:49:56.310
Feeling the pain. facing it...

794
00:49:57.812 --> 00:49:59.603
that takes courage.

795
00:49:59.605 --> 00:50:01.273
It's okay to let it out.

796
00:50:05.861 --> 00:50:06.904
It's okay.

797
00:50:11.325 --> 00:50:12.504
[SOBS]

798
00:50:20.334 --> 00:50:23.043
[OLIVIA] <i>Not a day passes
during this trial...</i>

799
00:50:23.045 --> 00:50:24.044
It's okay.

800
00:50:24.046 --> 00:50:26.088
<i>In the months it took to get here</i>

801
00:50:26.090 --> 00:50:29.550
<i>that I don't wish I could have
wrapped my arms around her</i>

802
00:50:29.552 --> 00:50:31.470
<i>and told her it would be okay.</i>

803
00:50:32.680 --> 00:50:34.265
<i>But I never had that chance.</i>

804
00:50:35.224 --> 00:50:37.309
Why didn't you tell us he was on drugs?

805
00:50:38.144 --> 00:50:39.914
He was getting better. okay?

806
00:50:39.917 --> 00:50:41.964
Anyway. I didn't even know about the

807
00:50:41.967 --> 00:50:43.147
drugs when I first brought him here.

808
00:50:43.149 --> 00:50:45.232
- Should we call social services?
- No. Dad!

809
00:50:45.234 --> 00:50:47.483
Call social services. he
disappears into the system.

810
00:50:47.484 --> 00:50:48.527
he doesn't testify.

811
00:50:48.529 --> 00:50:50.028
Jesus. is that what we care about?

812
00:50:50.030 --> 00:50:52.030
No. I care about keeping the kids safe.

813
00:50:52.032 --> 00:50:54.241
which is hard to do when
they're both fighting us.

814
00:50:54.243 --> 00:50:56.952
- How am I fighting you?
- The <i>Register</i> called me today. Clay.

815
00:50:56.954 --> 00:50:58.996
Those audio files were watermarked.

816
00:50:58.998 --> 00:51:00.706
You stole them from my computer.

817
00:51:00.708 --> 00:51:02.749
You told me you weren't
working on the case.

818
00:51:02.751 --> 00:51:05.085
- That's no excuse.
- You told Sonya.

819
00:51:05.087 --> 00:51:07.754
About Zach texting Hannah.
That's how they knew everything.

820
00:51:07.756 --> 00:51:08.714
Is that true?

821
